=================================================================
=              17.1 WILDFIRE: GROWING A SELECTION               =
=================================================================
 zmax parses the buffer with tree-sitter, so it knows where
 the expression under the cursor begins and ends.

 In normal mode, press Enter. The closest enclosing text
 object is selected. Press Enter again and the selection grows
 to the next one out: the argument, then the call, then the
 statement, then the block. Backspace shrinks it back.

 Try it on this line:

     print(compute(a, b) + offset)

 Put the cursor on b and press Enter three or four times.

 Because it is only a selection, any operator you already know
 (d, c, y, >) applies to whatever you grew.



=================================================================
=                       17.2 TEXT OBJECTS                       =
=================================================================
 A text object names a region without moving there first. In
 the default keymap it follows an operator or v :

   diw    delete the inner word
   ci"    change what is inside the quotes
   ya(    yank the parentheses and their contents
   vip    select the paragraph
   dit    delete the contents of the HTML or XML tag
   dif    delete the body of the function
   vaC    select the class or type around the cursor

 i means inner, a means around. The last two are tree-sitter
 objects: f function, C class, a parameter, c comment, T test,
 e entry, x XML element. They work in any language that has a
 grammar installed, with no per-language setup.

 In the helix preset the same objects are mi f and ma f .


=================================================================
=                    17.3 STRUCTURAL MOTIONS                    =
=================================================================
 The bracket keys jump by syntax rather than by line.

   ]m  [m     next / previous function or member
   ]/  [/     next / previous comment
   ]]  [[     next / previous section
   ]z  [z     end of the next fold / start of this one
   ])  [(     next / previous unmatched parenthesis
   ]}  [{     next / previous unmatched brace

 These are grammar-driven, so ]m lands on the next function in
 Rust, Python or Go alike.

 The helix preset spells the same family differently and adds
 more of it: ]f functions, ]t classes, ]a parameters,
 ]T tests, ]c comments, ]e entries, ]x XML elements.




=================================================================
=                   17.4 SIBLINGS AND PARENTS                   =
=================================================================
 The helix preset adds keys that walk the syntax tree itself:

   A-o        expand the selection to the parent node
   A-i        shrink it back to the child
   A-n  A-p   move to the next / previous sibling node
   A-a        select every sibling
   A-e  A-b   move to the end / start of the parent node

 In the default keymap SPC v expands the region, which is the
 same command under its spacemacs name, and Enter (wildfire)
 covers the common case of growing outward.

 :injections lists the embedded grammars in the buffer, such
 as the SQL inside a string or the JavaScript inside HTML.





